card.statement:
Let $\mathcal{C}$ be any subset of $\mathcal{R}$. Given $(k,i,j),\ (r,s,t)\in \mathfrak{V}(\mathcal{C})$ we will write:

- [(i)] $(k,i,j)\succeq_{\mathcal{C}} (r,s,t)$ if, there exists $\{(k_1,i_{1},j_{1}),\ldots,(k_m,i_{m},j_{m})\}\subseteq \mathfrak{V}(\mathcal{C})$ such that

\begin{align}
\{(k,i,j)\geq (k_1,i_{1},j_1), \cdots,\  (k_m,i_{m},j_m)\geq (r,s,t)\}&\subseteq \mathcal{C}
\end{align}

- [(ii)] We write $(k,i,j)\succ_{\mathcal{C}} (r,s,t)$ if there exists $\{(k_1,i_{1},j_{1}),\ldots,(k_m,i_{m},j_{m})\}\subseteq \mathfrak{V}(\mathcal{C})$ satisfying (<<ref:geq sub C>>), with one of the inequalities being $>$.
